# LF in every working tree, whatever core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows and
# the windows-latest runners default to autocrlf=true, and a CRLF checkout
# breaks things that work on macOS: Vitest doesn't strip a `#!...\r` shebang
# (scripts/check-contrast.mjs fails to parse under `npm run test`), and the
# shell scripts don't run under Git Bash with `\r` line ends.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
